]>
<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "6B">
<servcat sctnbr = "06" scnbr = "02">
<configtype typenbr = "0">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A6206013" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "01" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Steering Lock Removal and Installation
</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A6206013001">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<attention1>
<ptxt>
Steering lock is made of magnesium. 
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Drilling, cutting or filing the steering lock may spark to ignite magnesium powder, causing a fire or burn.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Do not perform drilling, cutting or filing magnesium powder on the steering lock.
</ptxt>
</attention1>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Failure to take the following precautions when removing or installing the steering lock can cause failure of the steering lock.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Do not drop or otherwise expose the steering lock to large shock. Any steering lock that has received large shock should be replaced.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Keep the steering column and/or the steering lock free of oil, water, dust or other foreign materials.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention4>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove steering column (1). 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A6206009"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Hold steering column using vise.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Loosen steering lock bolt(s) (2) using chisel, and then remove auto steering lock (3) from steering column.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A620006.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "44.346mm" ver = "01" gw = "98" gh = "109"/>
</figure>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A6206013002">
<title>
Installation
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A6206016">Auto Steering Lock Inspection</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install auto steering lock with the column cover mounting screw hole (1) toward P/S motor side.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A620007.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "47.344mm" ver = "01" gw = "223" gh = "118"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[a]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
P/S motor side
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Tighten new steering lock bolts (1) until head of each bolt is broken off.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGRA0A620004.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "44.555mm" ver = "01" gw = "212" gh = "110"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install steering column. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A6206009"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition to “ACC” or “ON” and check that steering shaft rotates smoothly. Then set ignition to “OFF” and check that steering wheel is locked.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check steering column and torque sensor after installation. If faulty condition is found, replace steering column.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Steering column: 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A6206011"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Torque sensor: 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A6306001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
</servinfo>
</servinfotype>
</configtype>
</servcat>
</section></manual></suzuki>
